ders will  come into force to control water usage  in certain areas the effects on wildlife  and farming would be catastrophic if no  preventative measures were taken and the  ground continued to heat up and we'd see  cracked land withered gardens and  parched reservoirs last seen in the  great drought of 1976. preserving the  uk's water levels is paramount although  water companies do have a sufficient  supply we have been told to use it  wisely
 

